 Runtime wire duplicate/reconnect paths remain separate from public API retry.
 
+The r7 all-M4 successor also makes capture disposal reentrant-safe. It first
+preflights every reference checkout without changing ownership, then marks the
+capture expired before disposing public drafts (which can invoke caller-owned
+revertible disposal callbacks). A callback that calls `capture.dispose()` again
+is a no-op. Transaction/change-event preflight failures leave the capture usable.
+Real teardown errors are not swallowed; internal A/S checkout cleanup runs in
+`finally`, and an already-started capture disposal remains expired.
+
